# Files NOT uploaded to Vercel. The Vercel CLI never reads .gitignore: it skips
# its own short list (.env.local and .env.*.local are on it, plain .env is not)
# plus what is written here.
#
# Environment values come from the Vercel project settings and from nowhere
# else. A deploy typed on a developer's machine would otherwise upload
# apps/web/.env, the build would read it, and every variable the project lacks
# would take its value from that file. While that file is the copy inherited
# from MedChina (CLAUDE.md, "Safety during the transition"), those values are
# another product's production credentials.
# scripts/preflight-env.test.mjs fails if these two lines go.
.env
.env.*
